    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 255 tests pass, including the `AcceptanceTest`. Let me summarize what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required a new read-only `telephoneDisplay` field: the stored E.164 `telephone` formatted for humans (country code, space, national digits grouped in threes, e.g. `+61 412 345 678`), while `telephone` stays raw E.164.\n\nThis project serves owners through a MapStruct-populated `OwnerDto` that is generated from `openapi.yml`, so the change spanned three coordinated edits:\n\n1. **`E164Telephone.java`** \u2014 added `toDisplayOrNull(String e164)`, a presentation-only formatter that reuses the existing `NATIONAL_LENGTH_BY_COUNTRY_CODE` table to split the country code from the national number, then groups the national digits in threes (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`). It returns `null` for anything that isn't a value the normalizer produces (no `+`, wrong digit count, or an unrecognized country code) \u2014 so seed owners whose stored telephone is still raw (e.g. `6085551023`) degrade gracefully rather than throwing.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"telephoneDisplay\", expression = \"java(telephoneDisplay(owner))\")` plus a `telephoneDisplay(owner)` default method delegating to the formatter, matching how every other derived owner field (displayName, initials, etc.) is wired.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `telephoneDisplay` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nThe raw `telephone` field is untouched (the display is a pure rendering). The existing `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` acceptance test passes (`telephone` = `+61412345678`, `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`), and the full suite is green: **255 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.",
